docs/cross-project/nedschorus-founding-plan.md:48:**The MD-GHI pair:** a request for a durable MD IS a request for a doc + issue pair (the boss's trigger word: "memorialize"). All NC-related GHIs — paired or issue-only — are filed on the nedschorus repository, never in the old system's tracker (boss-ruled 2026-07-22: NC context must not drown among the legacy system's thousands of issues). `md-write` searches existing pairs first, then disposes NEW / REVISE (default on subject match) / REPLACE (supersede, old issue closed same commit) / REMOVE; ambiguity goes to the `draft` issue queue, never blocks. Session provenance: MDs via commit messages; issues via a footer line. Revision convention (boss-ruled 2026-07-22): a clarification or revision to an issue or a pair document EDITS the artifact — the GHI body, the document — never a stacked clarifying comment; additive records multiply and conflict with what they meant to fix. Comments append only for genuinely new events (an instance outcome, a ruling challenge — "completion" collapsed into close-with-reason plus the body edit recording the outcome, user-ruled 2026-08-12). Append-only audit surfaces (review clearances and their trailers) are the deliberate exception. Artifact-lifecycle rule (boss-ruled 2026-07-24; supersedes and absorbs the 2026-07-23 three-state artifact rule): **every artifact is either final at its home, or sitting in a named queue that states its destination — and every queue has a drain process.** No stateless piles, ever. Destination known up front → destination-rooted queue: wiki-bound doctrine in `docs/wiki/queue/`, pair-bound MDs in `docs/issues/queue/` — the same `queue` token everywhere, so one grep finds every queue. Destination decided only at the drain → decision queue: `nc-queue/` (boss notes) and `legacy-feature-queue/` (undecided legacy features). Draft GHIs carry the **`draft` label** — the issue-world's queue membership, symmetric with the directories. The drain is one process for all queues ([nedschorus#24](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/24)): the boss walks a queue when he chooses; each item gets exactly one of four outcomes — **promote** (`git mv` to the destination; the move commit is the record), **edit** (revise, stays queued), **demote** (down to evidence/transient, attached to its pair or session), **drop** (deleted with the reason in the commit message — explicit, never silent rot). The handoff scrub step reports every queue's depth and oldest item; until the NC handoff skill is built, that reporting runs as discipline. Transient design/research MDs never enter these queues — they live and die attached to their pair or session. The absorbed three-state routing still governs write time: a queue drop needs NO GHI — the queue is its attention surface until the drain decides its fate, and minting a GHI at drop time front-runs the walk; the moment something is wanted as a feature, component, or commitment — any pending state — it gets a GHI (lean decision → issue-only; substantial working material → the MD-GHI pair: the MD carries the greppable substance, the GHI carries the walkable state); a bare MD with no GHI is legitimate only for final reference content awaiting nothing (operator notes beside code, wiki pages), and anything about it that later becomes pending gets a GHI then. Discriminator: the GHI carries state, the MD carries substance, the queue holds the not-yet-decided. Boss clarification 2026-07-25 (walk 17 cluster 2): **a committed doc is not an attention surface** — a backlog section or "captured research" note in a pair doc is a pile unless it is queued or carried by a GHI; anything task-shaped (an investigation, an evaluation, a build) gets a GHI even when small — lean bundled issues are fine; and agent-internal task lists are invisible to the boss until a review method exists ([nedschorus#28](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/28) item 5), so nothing may live only there. Enforced at write time by `ghi-write`/`md-write` ([nedschorus#13](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/13)).
docs/cross-project/nedschorus-founding-plan.md:69:**7. Pick ONE task; boot; run it; learn.** Ruled direction, CONFIRMED as the first bounded test task (walk item 15, 2026-07-25): the git foundation — the git-gatekeeper build slice (config + git-gatekeeper script with built-in checks + protection lock + workflow rules). Boot-test the delta first (find a named thing in the legacy system without writing there; use the bridge; produce a handoff — plus the founding interrogation probes: who are you; what are we building; what the legacy system is and its rules; hand off and resume; d-review a sample); every failure patches the pack. Then task 2 (standing candidate: the code-review skill), and companion admission right after the boot test passes. Candidate skills join one at a time when the running task exposes the missing decision (boot-set rule, open question 8) — the git-gatekeeper task's first expected pull is `write-test-plan` ([nedschorus#18](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/18)).
docs/cross-project/nedschorus-founding-plan.md:85:1. RESOLVED 2026-07-31 (number kept for reference stability): the entry-checkpoint statement is approved in its trailer-based form — no import can be checked in unrecorded, and the record cannot lag the system: `check-in` validates the declared `--import` triple at instant screening (each defect a named refusal) and writes the `Gatekeeper-import` trailer itself, same commit, with `imports` deriving the table from history ([git-gatekeeper-design.md](git-gatekeeper-design.md) § Constructive guarantees). Named residual (accepted): the guarantee binds declared imports; undeclared copying of legacy content is the cooperative-discipline class — governed by the rewrite policy (unexamined is never preserved) and caught at the walk.
docs/cross-project/nedschorus-founding-plan.md:86:2. RESOLVED 2026-07-31 as DROPPED (number kept for reference stability): the founding transcripts are not committed. The standing-decisions section above is the decision record — every ruling carries its date, substance, and reasoning — and capture-the-decision-never-the-meeting governs; committing raw conversations to a public repository buys hypothetical provenance at certain noise and S1-class exposure. Accepted residual: the raw generative reasoning stays machine-local and unbacked beyond Time Machine. Reopening trigger: a founding ruling genuinely disputed where the recorded decision proves insufficient — the transcripts either still exist locally then, or the ruling is re-derived and re-walked per the revision convention.
docs/cross-project/nedschorus-founding-plan.md:104:8. RESOLVED 2026-07-24 (number kept for reference stability): boot set = the five founding skills only (step 1); none of the nine candidate skills ([nedschorus#15](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/15)–[#23](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/23)) joins at boot. Candidates join one at a time, when a real task exposes the missing decision the candidate encodes; first expected pull: `write-test-plan` ([nedschorus#18](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/18)) at the step-7 git-gatekeeper task. Named-deferred classes — on the map, deliberately no GHI until their trigger occurs: `release-transition` and `learn-from-failure` (carried from the skills research), and `suite-health` (boss-ruled 2026-07-29, SDLC-note walk): the seven July-5 suite-operation skills (deflaker, repro-reducer, suite-tiering, skip-warden, golden/datadriven/property harness-writers) recorded as one deferred class, trigger being the first sustained test suite whose signal degrades; skip-warden's expiry-on-skips convention rides the first test-writing skill; test-diff-reviewer and test-ghostwriter are already covered by existing candidates.
