docs/issues/queue/21-diagnose-failure-test-procedure.md:32:Hard-to-repro production failures are diagnosed by instrumentation up the chain from the visible failure point — agent-duplicable (boundary instrumentation + the differencing above). The genuinely hard class (boss): design flaws, and one agent's failure to understand the large system around the code it sees. Status of countermeasures, stated precisely (new-vp flank correction, 2026-07-31): **one ruled countermeasure exists** — the broad-expert half of the reset pair, whose job is carrying the surrounding-system picture. The *doctrine* that explanatory architecture description is regenerated from code on demand and never carries authority is boss-ruled (queue note §6a item 1(b), 2026-07-29), but **no view-generation machinery or practice exists or is ruled** — "current architecture view on request" goes on the table as a candidate instance of that doctrine, not as existing machinery.
docs/issues/queue/35-declaration-vs-reality-posit-ladder.md:1:# Ladder extension for pair #35 (declaration-vs-reality) — the posit system at three granularities
docs/issues/queue/35-declaration-vs-reality-posit-ladder.md:3:Queued for the boss's drain (promote / edit / demote / drop). Source: `nc-queue/2026-07-28-sdlc-skill-set-coverage-and-app-skill-pile.md` §2 (rewalked) and §6a (boss-walked 2026-07-29/30). Destination: [nedschorus#35](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/35) — this extends that thread's primitive (declare expectation → observe reality → mismatch is red) down a granularity ladder; it is one system with one home, not a new thread. Status: direction with ruled structure; awaits a real codebase to instrument.
docs/issues/queue/35-declaration-vs-reality-posit-ladder.md:7:1. **System/path-class tags** (#35's existing subject): code tagged with expected firing class; both mismatch directions are alarms — EMERGENCY-ONLY firing weekly is a live incident detector; HOT never firing is a dead path or misroute.
docs/issues/queue/35-declaration-vs-reality-posit-ladder.md:8:2. **Branch classes (boss-ruled 2026-07-30):** every branch (CFG edge; one line may hold one decision of several conditions) carries a frequency-class posit — HOT / NORMAL / RARE / NEVER-except-emergency. Totality is a lintable exhaustiveness check. Numeric posits (relative to the enclosing function, e.g. "<1% of calls") only where the design states a frequency. Instruments split by question: event-based coverage (coverage.py on `sys.monitoring`, dynamic contexts) verifies existence and the RARE end via synthetic exercise; sampling (py-spy) verifies HOT/NORMAL distribution — sampling alone cannot distinguish cold from dead; tags remove that burden. Precedent: measurement side mature (PGO/gcov branch profiles); the declared-expectation side is novel — nearest is FoundationDB `CODE_PROBE` (binary reach); this is its quantitative generalization.
docs/issues/queue/35-declaration-vs-reality-posit-ladder.md:18:- **Pilot-measurement obligation (boss-ruled 2026-07-30)**: the first implementation measures whether every-branch positing stays within the goal framing — "not too token heavy" (write-time posit generation, storage, and check-time cost) — before the practice generalizes beyond the pilot. The every-branch ruling is conditional on that measurement, not assumed.
docs/issues/queue/35-declaration-vs-reality-posit-ladder.md:22:The boss's framing (2026-07-29): the hard problem is not removing obsolete code but determining what is used frequently versus never, and why — zero usage has four causes (lucky so far / superseded / flawed premise visible / flawed premise invisible) with four remedies; usage data finds candidates, the why is judgment. Companion improvements ruled in the same walk: design-change obsolescence sweep (pair #17 checklist line); patch-cycle tripwire generalized to a circuit breaker on closed agent loops (draft engineering rules queue).
docs/issues/queue/20-implement-with-evidence-agent-native-riders.md:3:Queued for the boss's drain (promote / edit / demote / drop). Source: `nc-queue/2026-07-28-sdlc-skill-set-coverage-and-app-skill-pile.md` §6a items 2 and 4 (boss-walked 2026-07-29/30). Destination: [nedschorus#20](https://github.com/nedschorus/nedschorus/issues/20).
docs/issues/queue/20-implement-with-evidence-agent-native-riders.md:5:1. **One-shot creators, retained for interrogation (boss-ruled).** Code and test writing is done by one-off agents: a creator's context is poisoned as a judge by its assumption of success, so it never reviews its own work. Its session ID (a short string; the transcript jsonl persists) is retained until the work clears checks **or 30 days elapse, whichever comes first** (boss-ruled 2026-07-30 — the interrogation window rides inside the drop discipline), so the creator can be resurrected as an **evidence source**: when a checker finds a problem, interrogate the creator with the blameless framing — "the goal is not an apology; was your instruction set confusing, incorrect, or lacking?" Findings land upstream (design text, skill prompts, wiki, CLAUDE.md), because every future agent inherits the same boot context — one context patch corrects the population.
docs/issues/queue/20-implement-with-evidence-agent-native-riders.md:7:3. **Branch-frequency posits written at implementation time (boss-ruled).** Every branch (control-flow-graph edge) gets a frequency-class posit (HOT / NORMAL / RARE / NEVER-except-emergency) written while the author-agent's context is fresh; numeric posits (relative to the enclosing function) only where the design states a frequency. Posits are predictions with provenance (design-claim ref or dated author-judgment) — written before consulting measurement. Full mechanics and mismatch verdicts: pair #35's ladder record.
docs/issues/queue/20-implement-with-evidence-agent-native-riders.md:9:4. **Bidirectional regression witness** (superpowers extract, 2026-07-31): a regression test's evidence cycle is write → pass → revert the fix → the test must fail → restore → pass. One direction proves the oracle can go red; both directions prove this test goes red for this fix. Mechanical (a stash/revert in the harness), applied when the witness is a test tied to a specific correction and a repro exists, at the fidelity category it honestly earned (minimal / partial / not-reproduced — see the #21 packet's procedure). Companion rule: an implementing agent's success claim is evidenced by the working-tree diff and check output, never by the agent's report alone.
docs/issues/queue/20-implement-with-evidence-agent-native-riders.md:11:5. **Fix mode is a distinct role (boss-ruled 2026-07-31)**: applying review findings is done by a third fresh one-shot agent — not the writer, not the reviewer — with a constructed context (design + code + tests + complete findings batch) and a trust-nothing briefing; full contract in the agent-loop draft rules (rule 5). No dedicated fix skill is created yet; one is pulled when the first real fix task exposes the need (boot-set rule).
