docs/issues/queue/3-gatekeeper-build-bindings.md:13:New instant-screening form error `unsafe-path`: refuses any path in `--files` or the import triple containing whitespace, `->`, non-printable, or non-ASCII bytes. Asymmetry justifies starting tight (relaxing later is forward-compatible; tightening later strands history); verified 2026-07-30: `git ls-files` in both repos shows zero matches on all three classes, so the rule costs nothing today. Growth path named, not built: a real unsafe-path import triggers git-style quoting then; the refusal's `next_action` says so. Parser stance on repeated `Gatekeeper-import:` lines (hand-pushed bypass class only): each line derives one row of the `imports` table. Tests: trailer round-trip via `git interpret-trailers` and the repeated-line assertion join T10; per-position unsafe-path cases join T11.
